      "local_deviation": "Cluster and ACP runner-pool administration remain visible as a native route contract in Local mode but require Cloud authority; registration tokens are never synthesized or cached by the renderer.",
      "judgment_rationale": "Cluster list and detail pages are direct sources for the canonical cluster control plane. Reads require tenant membership while cluster create, update, delete, ACP runner-pool creation and registration-token actions require tenant administration; the uncalled runner-pool update service method is not surface authority, and no cluster:read permission exists. Cloud Desktop has a real native loader, App binding, typed client and controller for paginated list reads, current-page search, filtering, refresh and health inspection, but workbenchCapabilityClient still wraps runtimeClustersCapability with declared renderer provenance. Snapshot v4 therefore closes Cloud to renderer_capability_authority_unobserved and promotes no action. Local Desktop keeps the native route shell but returns the stable not-applicable authority instead of simulating a cluster topology.",
