      "judgment_rationale": "InstanceTemplateList and TemplateDetail form a dedicated canonical lifecycle distinct from the general template marketplace. The production pages expose list, create, detail, list-items, delete, publish, clone, and deploy-from-template, and do not call update, unpublish, add-item, or remove-item APIs. Web is degraded because template calls and instance creation do not carry the route tenant while the backend resolves get_current_user_tenant from the user's first membership. Desktop has a real native loader, App binding, typed client, controller and lifecycle page, but workbenchCapabilityClient still wraps instanceTemplatesCapability with declared renderer provenance. Snapshot v4 therefore closes the active Cloud declaration to renderer_capability_authority_unobserved and exposes no route-reachable actions. Local renders the stable local_instance_template_authority_unavailable terminal state from the same declared renderer boundary; it has no observed sidecar template authority.",
